{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "וחזקתי", :translit "v'chizakti", :gloss "and I will harden / strengthen"} {:he "וחזקתי את זרועות מלך בבל", :translit "v'chizakti et z'rot melech bavel", :gloss "and I will strengthen the arms of the king of Babylon"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Word-count: the phrase וחזקתי appears twice in Scripture — here and in Ezekiel 30:24."}], :frame {:text "The verse states that God hardened Pharaoh's heart. The midrash addresses why Scripture uses language of divine strengthening against the wicked: when the Holy One, blessed be He, decrees punishment, He strengthens the wicked in their defiance so they fill their measure and are removed from the world (Shemot Rabbah 13:3). Ba'al HaTurim compresses this tradition by linking the two occurrences of וחזקתי — one regarding Pharaoh (Exodus 14:4), one regarding the king of Babylon (Ezekiel 30:24) — illustrating the same principle across two tyrants.", :sources ["Shemot Rabbah 13:3" "Exodus 14:4" "Ezekiel 30:24"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Word-count: the phrase וחזקתי appears twice in Scripture — here and in Ezekiel 30:24.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:15:39.760271219Z", :model "glm-5.2"}